 - Access: `docs/intent/access/access-design.md`, with `docs/intent/access/access-specs.md`. Written below the stable HTTPS command boundary.
-- Change store: `docs/intent/change-store/change-store-design.md`, with `docs/intent/change-store/change-store-specs.md`. Not written yet. Revision history, read indexes, and any publication outbox depend on the delivery approach.
-- Delivery: `docs/intent/delivery/delivery-design.md`, with `docs/intent/delivery/delivery-specs.md`. Not written yet. Owns polling responses, socket sessions, or hosted publication, depending on the approach.
-- Browser sync: `docs/intent/browser-sync/browser-sync-design.md`, with `docs/intent/browser-sync/browser-sync-specs.md`. Not written yet. Its subscription, reconnect, and catch-up behavior depend on the approach.
+- Change store: `docs/intent/change-store/change-store-design.md`, with `docs/intent/change-store/change-store-specs.md`. Not written yet. Stores each event's revisions in order, replayable from any revision inside the seven-day retention window, and publishes every committed revision to delivery so none is dropped while delivery is restarting.
+- Delivery: `docs/intent/delivery/delivery-design.md`, with `docs/intent/delivery/delivery-specs.md`. Not written yet. Owns WebSocket sessions and fan-out to browsers subscribed to an event, authenticates each connection through the access component, and owns connection capacity for 800 simultaneous browsers.
+- Browser sync: `docs/intent/browser-sync/browser-sync-design.md`, with `docs/intent/browser-sync/browser-sync-specs.md`. Not written yet. Subscribes per event, tracks the last applied revision, reconnects with backoff, and requests replay from that revision to catch up after a disconnect of up to 20 minutes.
 
