 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for committed-change delivery.** Delivery and browser sync run on infrastructure the project operates, with replayable per-event revisions for reconnect catch-up. Five-second polling was rejected for repeated reads and seconds of lag; a hosted realtime service was rejected for recurring fees and provider coupling. Accepted cost: connection capacity, reconnect handling, and replay are project-owned operations.
